    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-19 (D-1 C)">Scope: ordering. PRESCRIPTIVE and binding: the client re-point and the probe endpoint ship and deploy BEFORE any Create privilege is removed from any human role. Reversing it hides Manage Access for every user while the BFF's app-only write keeps working — a silent, total loss of the affordance.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 / spec.md FR-07">Scope: fail direction. The new client gate FAILS CLOSED — an unanswerable access question is a denial, matching `CallerRecordAccessProbe` (`:478`). Do NOT preserve the current fail-open "availability fallback"; inverting it is the point of this task, not a side effect.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Scope: the new endpoint. Resource authorization stays in an endpoint filter; the new route reports the caller's rights, it does not become a second enforcement point. The server's enforcement remains `DelegationRuleFilter` — this endpoint must never be the thing that permits a write.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: client auth. The probe call goes through `@spaarke/auth`'s `authenticatedFetch` (already bootstrapped in `init()` via `authInit.ts`), never a raw fetch with a hand-built Authorization header, and the endpoint runs OBO so it answers for the CALLER and not for the app.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Scope: the shared modal. `AccessGrantModal` stays entity-agnostic — it keeps receiving a boolean prop. Do not push entity names, record ids or probe calls into the shared component.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 114 lesson">Scope: tests. Ship the test WITH the code. `TrackingFieldTrio.toolbar.test.tsx:124` currently asserts "defaults the person icon to enabled when canGrantAccess is omitted" — that pins the retired default and MUST be updated in the same change. A green suite after changing only one side proves nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: the new endpoint. Reuse `CallerRecordAccessProbe` and `DataverseAccessRightsMapper`; do not write a second `RetrievePrincipalAccess` caller, and do not widen the endpoint into a general permissions API. One record, the caller, the rights.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement Justification for the new endpoint citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; publish size measured against a FRESH master worktree from a SHORT path with file counts compared on both sides; no new HIGH CVE; tests updated per §10 bullet 6.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md">Scope: PCF deployment. Bump the control version in all four locations and show it in the footer per `docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md`; build with `npm run build:prod`, never `npm run build`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="cross-project">Scope: coordination. Run `/conflict-check` even though `src/client/pcf/**` is not on the hot-path watchlist, and record in the task notes that this change supersedes `code-quality-and-assurance-r3`'s pcf-controls D7-01 as written, so that project's test is authored against fail-CLOSED.</constraint>
  </constraints>

